'' An intrinsic used as a value is typed, so PRINT can classify it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/intrinsic-expr-type.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered

'' LONG results print signed...
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_PrintInt
'' ...and SCREEN's ULONG prints UNSIGNED. Typing it LONG would use fb_PrintInt for
'' both and nothing would fail.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_PrintUInt

'' A string intrinsic hands back a descriptor, exactly as a string-returning call does.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_FileStrInput
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_PrintString
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_FileWstrInput

'' SINGLE and DOUBLE go to DIFFERENT entry points, and so do their prints.
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare f32 atan2f(f32 $0, f32 $1)
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare f64 atan2(f64 $0, f64 $1)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_PrintSingle
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_PrintDouble

'' The GOLDEN pins SCREEN's argument SWAP, which no substring can state.
'' GOLDEN: expected/intrinsic-expr-type.out
